  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="79dcc02b-722b-43fa-b175-5d7a3be32eb9"><problem><para>
      <para>The graph of function \(H\) shows the height, in meters, of a rocket \(t\) seconds after it was launched.
          <para><figure><media alt="Function on coordinate plane."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/45ceb267aeab7fc55ec544c03ba693d00323444a"/></media></figure></para>
          <para>Find \(H(0)\) in meters.</para>
          </para>
      <para> <emphasis> </emphasis></para>
    </para></problem><solution><para>15</para><para>
      <para>The correct answer is 15 meters. This is the height that the rocket was launched. </para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section></section>
</content>
